Can't say that I've ever seen this particular problem before, but I do 
have a lot of experience with the PWS's. First thing I'd do is check all 
the fans, she'll positively not boot if one of the cooling fans is dead.
Then I'd check the power supply, make sure the fan is blowing.
Then I'd check outputs, I'd look for +/- 5v & 12v on the plug to the 
motherboard.
Then I'd reseat the upper Motherboard and the memory.
Then I'd check each of the SCSI devices....
hmmm...
I seem to have rattled a loose brain cell!!!
I remember in the long dim past I had a CDRom drive fail that caused the 
system to not boot.  Try unplugging the CDRom.
After that I would simplify the system as best I could. I'd remove any 
and all SCSI devices, and any plug in cards that weren't absolutely 
necessary. I'd leave the video card in if you didn't have any experience 
of booting the system to the serial port.

Good luck!

TomC


