Sometimes I get a little confused with the documentation as it pertains 
to updating from floppy. Here is what is in the documentation:

2.2.3 Updating Using a FAT-Formatted Floppy Diskette

           Depending upon what you wish to update, you'll need either
           one or two 1.44MB floppy diskettes. If you wish to update
           console firmware only or I/O option firmware only, you'll
           need only a single diskette. However, if you wish to update
           both console and I/O firmware, you'll need two separate
           diskettes.

           Proper transfer type must be used when files are copied via
           ftp. Reference Section 1.6.1 for copying files, via ftp,
           that are to be used for FAT-format floppy updates.

